WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.940
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Welcome
to "Deconstructing Chatbots."

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.340
I am Priyanka Vergadia.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.940
And in this episode,
we are going

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.460
to explore how to
integrate Dialogflow

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.405
with Google Assistant.

00:00:09.405 --> 00:00:13.213
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.970
Once you build your
agent on Dialogflow,

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.010
you can use the
one-click integration

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.470
to connect to various
platforms, such as Google

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:29.910
Assistant, Slack, Facebook
Messenger, Twitter, and more.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:33.020
Today, we are going to look
at integrating Dialogflow

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.820
with Actions on Google.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.590
Actions on Google
is a platform where

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:40.040
you can create software to
extend the functionality

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.480
of Google Assistant.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:45.140
By integrating Dialogflow
with Actions on Google,

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:48.110
you can reach over
500 million devices

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:52.650
that support Google Assistant,
such as smart speakers, phones,

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.580
cars, TVs, or watches.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.580
Let's consider the same
appointment scheduler chatbot

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:01.220
that we built in the
previous episode and work

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.500
through the integration.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.959
Click on Integrations.

00:01:04.959 --> 00:01:07.860
We are going to explore Google
Assistant integration today.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.860
So let's just click that.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.760
In the pop-up window, we
define Explicit Invocation.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.160
What intent do we
want to trigger

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.390
when a user says, OK, Google,
talk to Smart Scheduler?

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:23.220
Smart Scheduler here
is our trigger name.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:26.030
We will see where to set
it up in just a little bit.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:28.880
In our case, Welcome
Intent is the perfect spot

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.660
for the user to land on.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.840
So we will just stick to that.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:35.060
Let's say a user
says, OK, Google,

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.030
ask Smart Scheduler to set
an appointment for 5:00

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.500
PM tomorrow.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.970
That is an implicit invocation.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:45.860
So in this case, we could invoke
our Schedule Appointment intent

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:51.020
directly, since we know exactly
what the user wants to do.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.090
If we want the
service to be only

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.580
available for signed-in
users, then you

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:58.010
can check the Sign-In
Required button.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.260
In our case, it's just
a demo, so we will just

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.810
keep it open to everybody.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.720
We are then going to
click on Test First.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:09.320
Since we just developed our
app, let's see how it functions,

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.194
or if it functions correctly.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.960
OK, that looks great.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:34.070
Now let's explore the
Manage Assistant App button.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:38.260
This provides us to set up the
invocation name to our chatbot.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.470
We called it Smart Scheduler.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:46.350
This is also the place to
select male or female voice

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.150
for your assistant.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:52.110
Going back to Overview, we have
already built our application.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.270
And it's ready to test.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.320
When you are ready
for deployment,

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.760
make sure you have selected the
countries you want to deploy in

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.400
and the surfaces you want
your actions to run on.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.750
You will have to
provide a description

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.240
for your application,
Sample Invocations.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.480
For example, here we've added
Talk to Smart Scheduler.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:14.260
You can add more.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.550
It also requires two images--

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:22.010
one small and one large.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.500
Contact details and
privacy information

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:27.340
fill up all those things.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.290
Once you have done
all that and feel

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:32.200
comfortable to push the
application to production,

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.500
use the Release option
to submit to production.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.990
Of course, here, we have not
finished the overviewed items.

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:42.700
So we don't have the ability
to submit to production yet.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:45.280
You can also enable
the launch in beta

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.030
to open it up for
up to 200 users.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:51.700
With alpha release, you
can enable your action

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.950
for up to 20 users without
submitting for review.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:56.450
All right.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:59.440
So today, we used our
Appointment Scheduler chatbot

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.480
that we built in
the previous episode

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:04.750
and integrated it with
Actions on Google.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.750
Don't miss the next episode
of deconstructing chatbots,

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.760
because we are going
to make our appointment

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.710
scheduler a little bit smarter.

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:15.360
[MUSIC PLAYING]

